PART I — THE 10/10 SCORECARD

This is our gate.

A build does not get called elite because it looks cool.

It gets scored across the following:

Category	Weight
1. Immediate Understanding	12%
2. Push-Button Simplicity	12%
3. Interaction / Living Responsiveness	12%
4. Visual Excellence & Craft	11%
5. Power Player Experience	10%
6. Navigation & Spatial Architecture	9%
7. Mobile & Responsive Experience	9%
8. Emotional Impact / Wow	8%
9. Accessibility & Inclusivity	6%
10. Performance & Technical Quality	6%
11. Consistency / Design System Integrity	5%
TOTAL	100%

And every category is scored:

0–3 = Poor
4–5 = Functional
6–7 = Good
8 = Excellent
9 = Elite
10 = World-class

But here's the important part:

Aesthetic beauty cannot compensate for poor usability.

A gorgeous interface that confuses someone gets a bad score.

A simple interface that looks dead gets a bad score.

A spectacular animation that slows someone down gets a bad score.

A perfect NayaNET experience has to win everywhere simultaneously.

